module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Constructible.SetSheafPresentationColimits
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Restriction.ShriekConstantFree
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Module sheaves are generated by the quasi-compact quasi-separated étale objects

Let `S` be a site with a distinguished collection of objects which covers it — condition (1) of
Stacks 0937 — and let `P U` be a sheaf of `R`-modules corepresenting sections over `U`, for each
object `U` of the site. Then the sheaves `P U` with `U` distinguished generate: every sheaf of
`R`-modules on the site is a quotient of a direct sum of them. On the small étale site of a scheme
`X`, with the quasi-compact quasi-separated étale objects as the distinguished collection and
`j_{U!}\underline{\Lambda}_U` as the corepresenting sheaves, this is Stacks 093B part (2) for
sheaves of `Λ`-modules.

The index set of the direct sum is the set of pairs `(U, s)` of a *distinguished* object and a
section of the sheaf over it, and that restriction is the whole point: the unrestricted statement,
`AlgebraicGeometry.epi_desc_moduleShriekConstant`, indexes over every étale object, whereas the
compactness that Stacks 093C needs of the generators holds only at the quasi-compact ones.

Cutting the index set down costs the sheaf condition on the target. Two morphisms out of a sheaf
agreeing on all sections over distinguished objects agree on all sections, because a section over
an arbitrary object restricts to sections over the members of a covering by distinguished objects
and a sheaf is separated; this is
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.hom_ext_of_coyonedaSections_of_hasEnoughObjects`, which replaces
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.hom_ext_of_coyonedaSections` and is the only new ingredient.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.hom_ext_of_coyonedaSections_of_hasEnoughObjects` — a family of sheaves
  corepresenting sections at a covering collection of objects is jointly epimorphic.
* `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.exists_epi_sigma_of_coyonedaSections` — hence every sheaf of modules on
  such a site is a quotient of a direct sum of those sheaves, indexed by pairs of a distinguished
  object and a section over it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_epi_sigma_moduleShriekConstant_qcqs` — **Stacks 093B part (2)** for
  sheaves of `Λ`-modules on the small étale site of a scheme: every such sheaf is a quotient of a
  direct sum of the sheaves `j_{U!}\underline{\Lambda}_U` at quasi-compact quasi-separated étale
  objects `U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.smallEtaleHasSheafifyModuleMax` — presheaves of `Λ`-modules on the small
  étale site of a scheme admit sheafification at the coefficient universe `max (u + 1) r`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.smallEtaleHasColimitsOfSizeModuleMax` — sheaves of `Λ`-modules on the small
  étale site of a scheme have all colimits of size `max (u + 1) r`.

## Implementation notes

Nothing is assumed about `X` beyond its being an object of the big étale site. Stacks 093B asks
only for condition (1) of its situation, that the distinguished objects cover; on the small étale
site the quasi-compact quasi-separated objects do so whatever `X` is, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.hasEnoughObjects_quasiCompactObjectsSituation`, so the
quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `X` that Stacks 03SA carries do not enter here.

The coefficient universe is pinned to `u + 1` for `B : AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleSite.{u}`, as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.epi_desc_moduleShriekConstant`: the small étale site of `X` is a `Type (u + 1)`
with `Category.{u}`, and the corepresentation
`AlgebraicGeometry.moduleShriekConstantCoyonedaIso` of sections by
`AlgebraicGeometry.moduleShriekConstant` is available only there.

The sheafification instance is supplied by the local instance `smallEtaleHasSheafifyModuleMax`,
which is `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.hasSheafify_moduleCat` at the universes above; it is needed
already to state the direct sum, and `HasSheafify` being a proposition it agrees with whatever
instance `AlgebraicGeometry.moduleShriekConstant` was elaborated with.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 093B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0937](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0937)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe v u r w

attribute [local instance 2000] Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfShape Sheaf.instHasFiniteCoproducts

namespace CategoryTheory.Sheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]

/-- The pairs `(U, s)` of a distinguished object of the site and a section of `F` over it. This is
the index set of the direct sum of Stacks 093B. -/
public abbrev DistinguishedSections (S : Stacks.QuasiCompactObjectsSituation C)
    (R : Type r) [Ring R] (F : Sheaf S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)) :
    Type max u v w :=
  Σ U : {U : C // U ∈ S.objects},
    (forget (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)).obj (F.obj.obj (op U.1))

/-- **A family of sheaves corepresenting sections at a covering collection of objects is jointly
epimorphic.** Let the distinguished objects of `S` cover every object of the site and let `P U`
corepresent sections over `U`. Then two morphisms out of a sheaf `F` which agree after every
morphism `P U ⟶ F` with `U` distinguished are equal.

A morphism `P U ⟶ F` is a section of `F` over `U`, so the hypothesis says that the two morphisms
agree on all sections over distinguished objects. An arbitrary section restricts to such sections
along a covering by distinguished objects, and the target, being a sheaf, is separated. -/
public theorem hom_ext_of_coyonedaSections_of_hasEnoughObjects
    (S : Stacks.QuasiCompactObjectsSituation C) (hEnough : S.HasEnoughObjects)
    (R : Type r) [Ring R] (P : C → Sheaf S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R))
    (ε : ∀ U, coyoneda.obj (op (P U)) ≅
      (sheafSections S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)).obj (op U) ⋙
        forget (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R))
    {F G : Sheaf S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)} (a b : F ⟶ G)
    (h : ∀ U ∈ S.objects, ∀ φ : P U ⟶ F, φ ≫ a = φ ≫ b) : a = b := by
  have key : ∀ U ∈ S.objects, a.hom.app (op U) = b.hom.app (op U) := by
    intro U hU
    ext s
    have hs : ∀ c : F ⟶ G, (ε U).hom.app G ((ε U).inv.app F s ≫ c) = c.hom.app (op U) s := by
      intro c
      have := NatTrans.naturality_apply (ε U).hom c ((ε U).inv.app F s)
      rwa [show (coyoneda.obj (op (P U))).map c ((ε U).inv.app F s)
        = (ε U).inv.app F s ≫ c from rfl, Iso.inv_hom_id_app_apply] at this
    rw [← hs a, h U hU, hs b]
  apply Sheaf.hom_ext
  apply NatTrans.ext
  funext ⟨V⟩
  obtain ⟨𝒰, h𝒰, hmem⟩ := hEnough V
  have harrows : Sieve.ofArrows 𝒰.X 𝒰.f ∈ S.topology V := by
    simpa only [PreZeroHypercover.sieve₀] using h𝒰
  refine G.property.hom_ext_ofArrows 𝒰.f harrows fun i => ?_
  rw [← a.hom.naturality (𝒰.f i).op, ← b.hom.naturality (𝒰.f i).op, key _ (hmem i)]

/-- **Stacks 093B part (2) at the level of sites.** Let the distinguished objects of `S` cover
every object of the site and let `P U` corepresent sections over `U`. Then every sheaf of
`R`-modules on the site is a quotient of the direct sum of the sheaves `P U` over all pairs
`(U, s)` of a distinguished object and a section over it, the component at `(U, s)` being the
morphism that `s` is.

The direct sum maps onto `F` because the morphisms `P U ⟶ F` with `U` distinguished are jointly
epimorphic, which is
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.hom_ext_of_coyonedaSections_of_hasEnoughObjects`. -/
public theorem exists_epi_sigma_of_coyonedaSections
    (S : Stacks.QuasiCompactObjectsSituation C) (hEnough : S.HasEnoughObjects)
    (R : Type r) [Ring R] [HasWeakSheafify S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)]
    (P : C → Sheaf S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R))
    (ε : ∀ U, coyoneda.obj (op (P U)) ≅
      (sheafSections S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)).obj (op U) ⋙
        forget (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R))
    (F : Sheaf S.topology (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)) :
    ∃ (A : Type max u v w) (U : A → C), (∀ a, U a ∈ S.objects) ∧
      ∃ p : (∐ fun a => P (U a)) ⟶ F, Epi p := by
  refine ⟨DistinguishedSections S R F, fun q => q.1.1, fun q => q.1.2,
    Limits.Sigma.desc fun q => (ε q.1.1).inv.app F q.2, ⟨fun {G} x y hxy => ?_⟩⟩
  refine hom_ext_of_coyonedaSections_of_hasEnoughObjects S hEnough R P ε x y fun U hU φ => ?_
  have hφ : Limits.Sigma.ι (fun q : DistinguishedSections S R F => P q.1.1)
        ⟨⟨U, hU⟩, (ε U).hom.app F φ⟩ ≫
      Limits.Sigma.desc (fun q : DistinguishedSections S R F => (ε q.1.1).inv.app F q.2) = φ := by
    rw [Limits.Sigma.ι_comp_desc, Iso.hom_inv_id_app_apply]
  rw [← hφ, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hxy]

end CategoryTheory.Sheaf

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Presheaves of `Λ`-modules on the small étale site of `X` admit sheafification, at the
coefficient universe `max (u + 1) r` at which the extensions by zero of constant module sheaves
corepresent sections. This is `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.hasSheafify_moduleCat` with its third
universe pinned to the ring universe, so that it applies as an instance. -/
public theorem smallEtaleHasSheafifyModuleMax (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (X : B.Scheme)
    (Λ : Type r) [CommRing Λ] :
    HasSheafify (SmallEtale.topology B X.1 X.property) (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) r} Λ) :=
  SmallEtale.hasSheafify_moduleCat.{u, r, r} B X Λ

/-- Sheaves of `Λ`-modules on the small étale site of `X` have all colimits of size
`max (u + 1) r`, module-valued sheaves inheriting the colimits of their coefficient category. -/
public theorem smallEtaleHasColimitsOfSizeModuleMax (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (X : B.Scheme)
    (Λ : Type r) [CommRing Λ] :
    HasColimitsOfSize.{max (u + 1) r, max (u + 1) r}
      (Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B X.1 X.property) (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) r} Λ)) :=
  let : HasColimitsOfSize.{max (u + 1) r, max (u + 1) r} (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) r} Λ) :=
    inferInstance
  CategoryTheory.Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfSize

attribute [local instance] smallEtaleHasSheafifyModuleMax

/-- **Stacks 093B part (2) for sheaves of `Λ`-modules on the small étale site.** Every sheaf of
`Λ`-modules on the small étale site of a scheme `X` is a quotient of a direct sum
`⊕ j_{U_a!}\underline{\Lambda}_{U_a}` of extensions by zero of constant free rank-one module
sheaves at *quasi-compact quasi-separated* étale objects `U_a` of `X`.

The source takes the objects of the direct sum from a collection which covers the site and
consists of quasi-compact objects; on the small étale site that collection is the quasi-compact
quasi-separated étale objects, which cover every étale object by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.hasEnoughObjects_quasiCompactObjectsSituation`. Maps out of
`j_{U!}\underline{\Lambda}_U` are sections over `U` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.moduleShriekConstantCoyonedaIso`, so the index set is the pairs of a
quasi-compact quasi-separated étale object and a section of the sheaf over it.

This strengthens `AlgebraicGeometry.epi_desc_moduleShriekConstant`, whose direct sum runs over all
étale objects, and it is the generation step of Stacks 093C for sheaves of modules: compactness of
the generators, `AlgebraicGeometry.isFinitelyPresentable_moduleShriekConstant`, is available
exactly at the quasi-compact objects. -/
@[stacks 093B "part (2), sheaves of modules, generation by qcqs étale objects"]
public theorem exists_epi_sigma_moduleShriekConstant_qcqs (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (X : B.Scheme)
    (Λ : Type r) [CommRing Λ]
    (F : Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B X.1 X.property) (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) r} Λ)) :
    ∃ (A : Type max (u + 1) r) (U : A → SmallEtale B X.1 X.property),
      (∀ a, IsQCQSEtaleObject B X (U a)) ∧
        ∃ p : (∐ fun a => moduleShriekConstant.{u, r, r} B X Λ (U a)) ⟶ F, Epi p :=
  Sheaf.exists_epi_sigma_of_coyonedaSections.{u, u + 1, r, r}
    (SmallEtale.quasiCompactObjectsSituation B X)
    (SmallEtale.hasEnoughObjects_quasiCompactObjectsSituation B X) Λ
    (fun U => moduleShriekConstant.{u, r, r} B X Λ U)
    (fun U => moduleShriekConstantCoyonedaIso.{u, r, r} B X Λ U) F

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
